HST Office: the File tab opens a drop-down panel ("Tệp tin") instead of the full-window File view.

The File view no longer hides the ribbon and no longer covers the document. It is a panel in a window of its own
that drops down under the ribbon, like a menu:

- sfx2/source/backstage/hstbackstagewindow.*: BackstageWindow is now the content of a weld::Popover (GtkPopover
  "HstFilePanel" in hstbackstage.ui), built for the document's top-level window and shown with popup_at_rect. GTK
  shows it in a popup window of its own under X11 (GtkInstancePopover) and as a GtkPopover under Wayland; the other
  VCL plugins (Windows, macOS, gen, Qt) show it in a floating popup window (SalInstancePopover). Its top edge is the
  bottom edge of the NotebookBar (the top of the document area without one), 8 px from the window's left edge; about
  780 x 580 at 100 %, scaled with the UI scale and kept inside the window and the screen below the ribbon, so it never
  opens upwards over the ribbon.
- Nothing of the frame is hidden or replaced: SetRibbonVisible, the child window over the client area and its resize
  handling are gone. The document stays on screen and live. The panel shows no image of the document; print preview
  stays in the Print dialog.
- It closes on Esc and on a click outside (the popover's own light dismiss), on Alt+F, and before any of its commands
  runs; the focus goes back to the document. The "←" item is gone: the footer says how to close the panel.
- Same 12 items, order and labels in the left column, now a light column with the command icons (a drawn house for
  Home) and the selection marked by a bar in the application colour; top edge in the application colour.
- The .uno:HSTBackstage label is "Bảng Tệp tin" (the panel, not a page). Info shows "—" for an empty value.
- Compact pages: four tiles on Home, narrower recent lists, and on New a list of this application's templates (all
  template folders, as the Templates dialog lists them) instead of the thumbnail gallery; Manage Templates… and
  Browse… open the full dialogs. Info keeps Properties…, Digital Signatures… and USB Token Setup….
- sfx2/source/backstage/hstbackstage.cxx: the panels are kept per frame (created on first use, removed when the frame
  is disposed) instead of being found among the children of the container window.
- Keyboard: the key handling of the former PreNotify is a key-press handler of the panel (arrows, Home, End, Right
  into the page, the frame's shortcuts). Widgets that the code hides are no-show-all, because the GTK popup window
  shows its contents with show_all. The .ui children carry no packing position: they are in their visual order, and
  VclBuilder (Windows, macOS, gen) put some of them out of order inside the popover. The anchor is in frame-window
  coordinates for GTK and in the frame's client window for the other plugins, as each popover expects.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/check-backstage.py, tests/runtime/check-backstage-flows.py.
